WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.400
As you first start fooling around on the internet back in the day, particularly on social media

00:03.400 --> 00:07.320
and online shopping platforms, there have been private data companies building an individual

00:07.320 --> 00:11.880
profile on you to sell to advertisers and corporations like Oracle who build regional

00:11.880 --> 00:15.040
and market specific algorithms based on consumer data.

00:15.040 --> 00:16.040
And guess what?

00:16.040 --> 00:17.040
You're the consumer pal.

00:17.040 --> 00:19.240
For a long time, this could have been seen as all fun and games.

00:19.240 --> 00:23.640
You buy a poolside basketball hoop on Amazon one day and then get served a whole gang of

00:23.640 --> 00:25.760
LeBron James highlights the next.

00:25.760 --> 00:26.760
It was chill.

00:26.760 --> 00:28.880
But now it's getting freaking scary.

00:28.880 --> 00:34.680
Three days ago, on March 18th, 2026, FBI Director Cash Patel sat before the Senate Intelligence

00:34.680 --> 00:39.600
Committee and confirmed, under oath, that the FBI is actively purchasing Americans'

00:39.600 --> 00:44.080
data in bulk from these same private data companies who'd worked in the ad space before

00:44.080 --> 00:46.560
to create domestic profiles on American shoppers.

00:46.560 --> 00:51.760
And what these data brokers have is a full dossier built from your entire digital footprint

00:51.760 --> 00:55.680
from your first MySpace profile in fourth grade to whatever the frick you're doing

00:55.680 --> 00:57.000
online right now.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.400
MySpace, to me and many other people, is seen as a bit concerning.

01:00.400 --> 01:02.720
You know, why does the FBI want all of our data?

01:02.720 --> 01:06.880
Are they developing some kind of dissident database to map and classify people who speak

01:06.880 --> 01:08.440
out against the federal government?

01:08.440 --> 01:12.960
Or maybe uncomfortable with the Epstein class forcing Americans to fight a war on behalf

01:12.960 --> 01:16.760
of a country that's bought and blackmailed its way into our political and media establishment

01:16.760 --> 01:20.520
with the sole purpose of manufacturing consent to expand their colonial project?

01:20.520 --> 01:21.520
I don't know.

01:21.520 --> 01:22.520
Hard to say.

01:22.520 --> 01:23.520
But I do know this.

01:23.520 --> 01:27.960
Obviously, keeping track of dissent in a country this large would have been a huge undertaking.

01:27.960 --> 01:32.480
But now, with powerful AI tools, it's not super hard for federal bodies like the FBI,

01:32.480 --> 01:37.520
ICE or CBP to do that, especially after Palantir, Peter Thiel's super chill company, had just

01:37.520 --> 01:42.080
formalized a $1.3 billion deal with the Pentagon, establishing Palantir as the default core

01:42.080 --> 01:44.720
AI system across all branches of the military and federal government.

01:44.720 --> 01:45.720
So that's where we're at.

01:45.720 --> 01:49.960
Pete Haggsest can build a big old cracker barrel in Damascus in 2050, and the edge of

01:49.960 --> 01:53.640
death, dinosaur humans making these calls for us right now won't even be around for

01:53.640 --> 01:54.800
the ribbon cutting ceremony.

01:54.800 --> 01:55.800
But I will channel five.

